On wasm32, ptrdiff_t is `long` (not `int`), but sizeof(long) == sizeof(int)
so PTRDIFF_MAX == INT_MAX. Scintilla's explicit template instantiations at
the bottom of RunStyles.cpp only cover <ptrdiff_t, X> when
PTRDIFF_MAX != INT_MAX, leaving <long, int> (used via Sci::Position in
Decoration.cpp) uninstantiated. Add them unconditionally for wasm.

Same idiom is used elsewhere in Scintilla for CellBuffer, ContractionState,
etc., but only RunStyles surfaced as an unresolved symbol so far.

--- a/libs/qscintilla_2.14.1/scintilla/src/RunStyles.cpp
+++ b/libs/qscintilla_2.14.1/scintilla/src/RunStyles.cpp
@@ -311,3 +311,7 @@ template class Scintilla::RunStyles<int, char>;
 template class Scintilla::RunStyles<ptrdiff_t, int>;
 template class Scintilla::RunStyles<ptrdiff_t, char>;
 #endif
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+template class Scintilla::RunStyles<long, int>;
+template class Scintilla::RunStyles<long, char>;
+#endif
